                <pb facs="1151" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5550: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-30T11:00:00+08:00">July 30, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 30—3 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>472. Reuter reports from Shanghai 29th: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“T. V. Soong, Minister of Finance, published warning this afternoon that
                            bonds secured on customs revenue issued by Canton rebels will not be
                            recognized in any way by the Government as having claim on national
                            funds. Statement points out that Canton rebels in proposing to issue
                            premium bonds secured on the additional customs duties are not only
                            infringing upon integrity of the customs service but are usurping
                            recognized rights of bondholders of foreign and national obligations. It
                            is emphasized that these obligations are secured on the customs revenue
                            as a whole and not on any specific part of it.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
